# SEO Conventions

Laferla Sports targets two search themes, both South Africa focused:

1. "ISSF / Capapie precision shooting equipment" (rifle & pistol)
2. "Capapie Trap & Skeet / shotgun shooting gear" (vests, inners, bags, gun covers)

Every page and product must reinforce one of them. Source of truth: `lib/seo.ts`.

## Every page MUST export `metadata` (or `generateMetadata`)

- `title`: unique, keyword-led. The layout adds the `| Laferla Sports` suffix via template — do NOT repeat the brand.
- `description`: 120–160 chars, includes a target phrase ("ISSF", "Capapie", "South Africa") where natural.
- `alternates.canonical`: set the canonical path (e.g. `/shop/<slug>`).
- Add `openGraph` for product/landing pages (title, description, image).

```tsx
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Shooting Jackets & Trousers', // -> "Shooting Jackets & Trousers | Laferla Sports"
  description: 'ISSF-compliant Capapie shooting jackets & trousers, in South Africa. Request a quote.',
  alternates: { canonical: '/shop/jackets-and-trousers' },
};
```

## Products MUST render structured data

Use `<ProductJsonLd product={product} />` on product pages.

The site is quote-based and publishes no prices, so `Product` schema deliberately
omits `offers`, `availability`, `sku` (unless Capapie publishes a real item code),
`aggregateRating` and `review`. Never add a placeholder price to regain rich-result
eligibility — a fabricated `price: 0` renders as "free" in search.

Pages with a breadcrumb trail should use `<Breadcrumbs />`, which emits
`BreadcrumbList` structured data alongside the visible nav.

## Images

- Every `<Image>`/`SafeProductImage` needs a descriptive `alt` (product name + context). Never `alt=""` on meaningful images.
- Product data carries `image_alt`; prefer it over falling back to the bare product name.

## Catalogue & routes

- Read products through `lib/catalog.ts`, not the individual data files.
  `lib/capapie-products.ts` is **generated** by `pnpm scrape-products`;
  `lib/shotgun-products.ts` is hand-authored from the Capapie brochure.
- Precision categories live at `/shop/<category-slug>`; shotgun categories live at
  `/shop/shotgun/<slug>` (see `lib/shotgun-categories.ts`) so the two taxonomies can
  reuse names like "Accessories" without colliding.
- All product detail pages stay flat at `/shop/<product-slug>` regardless of discipline.
- Any new public route must be added to `app/sitemap.ts`.

## Locale

- The site is `en-ZA`. Use South African English spelling (authorised, colour, programme) in copy.
